From: Oreon Packaging Team <packaging@oreonhq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] test3300: wait for the detached worker in release builds

The last pool in unit3300 is destroyed without a join, so its worker
is detached and still running. Only DEBUGBUILD waited for it to end,
so a release build returns from main with the worker alive and
valgrind reports its pthread TLS as possibly lost.

Wait in every build.
---
--- a/tests/unit/unit3300.c
+++ b/tests/unit/unit3300.c
@@ -142,13 +142,13 @@
   Curl_thrdpool_destroy(tpool, FALSE);
   fail_unless(ctx.returned < ctx.total, "pool-e returned all");
   fail_unless(ctx.taken < ctx.total, "pool-e took all");
-#ifdef DEBUGBUILD
   /* pool thread notices destruction and should immediately abort.
    * No memory leak should be reported. if the wait is too short on
    * a slow system, thread sanitizer freaks out as memdebug
-   * is called by threads after main thread shut down. */
+   * is called by threads after main thread shut down. Release builds
+   * need the wait too, or valgrind sees the detached worker still alive
+   * at exit and its TLS as possibly lost. */
   curlx_wait_ms(1000);
-#endif
 
   UNITTEST_END_SIMPLE
 }
